Why each additional element?

    * 2nd HAProxy (cluster):
        The previous infrastructure had the load balancer as a SPOF.
        With two HAProxy in active-passive cluster, if HAProxy 1 goes down, HAProxy 2 takes over automatically.
        No more single point of failure at the entry point
    
    * Dedicated web server (Nginx):
        Separating Nginx onto its own machine means it no longer competes for CPU and RAM with the application or the database.
        It can also be scaled independently if static traffic increases.

    * Dedicated application server:
        The business logic runs in isolation.
        If the app needs more resources, you scale only that server without touching the web server or the database.

    * Dedicated database server:
        MySQL gets its own resources, disk I/O, RAM, CPU, without interference from Nginx or the app.
        Database performance is critical, it should never share a machine with other components.